WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.190
Is your contract BUILT to last?

2
00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:03.890
Let's find out...

3
00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:05.390
with a blueprint.

4
00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:07.880
First — we BUILD.

5
00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:09.920
Six foundation blocks:

6
00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:13.920
parties, offer, acceptance,

7
00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:18.200
agreement, intention, capacity.

8
00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:20.400
Miss just ONE...

9
00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:22.200
and nothing stands.

10
00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:24.730
Then — the inspection.

11
00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:27.170
A crack in the FOUNDATIONS?

12
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.570
Void. It never stood at all.

13
00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:32.230
A crack in the walls?

14
00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:35.110
Voidable... repair it,

15
00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:36.270
or condemn it.

16
00:00:36.790 --> 00:00:40.140
Inspectors hunt for six defects.

17
00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:45.260
Illegality. Error. Misrepresentation.

18
00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:48.460
Capacity. Unfair terms...

19
00:00:49.310 --> 00:00:51.500
and restrictive covenants.

20
00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:53.490
And one day,

21
00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:54.650
it comes down.

22
00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:56.570
Usually by performance...

23
00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:58.950
but also by agreement,

24
00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:01.830
by a new deal — or

25
00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:02.970
when time runs out.

26
00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:05.460
And if someone knocks it down

27
00:01:05.310 --> 00:01:07.320
early? That's breach.

28
00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:09.580
You can claim damages...

29
00:01:09.430 --> 00:01:13.200
or ask the court to step

30
00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:13.520
in.

31
00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:15.090
Build it right.

32
00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:16.430
Inspect it hard.

33
00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:18.730
That's how a contract is...

34
00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:19.810
built to last.
